    "cross_source_insight": "Combining evidence from professional interviews (Andrew Cohen, Walter Trarbach) and AI research (AuraLuxMuse), it becomes clear that the human-centric, spatial, and narrative-sensitive aspects of stage design form a critical framework within which AI tools must operate. These tools can accelerate technical tasks like lighting cue generation but cannot substitute the creative iteration and live adaptation essential to theatre.",
    "limitation_highlight": "Current AI systems for lighting design, including AuraLuxMuse, face the limitation of lacking standardized parameterization and comprehensive evaluation benchmarks, constraining their ability to generalize beyond controlled scenarios and to fully automate high-level artistic decisions."
